			<div class="content" id="post-content-4449472">
									

<p>Thank you for the line-by-line. I've always struggled with these kinds of horror pieces, and I appreciate having someone go through it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I went through and fixed the problems you pointed out. As for the fact that it's a spider&#8230; I decided to make it a millipede. Imagining having all of those legs crawl over your brain. (In addition, they have a much simpler diet, which takes care of those bits :-) )</p>
<p>I'm not sure what to do about the interview; it's hard to write a convincing 10-year-old. I feel like anything else would feel unnecessarily expository.</p>
<p>For the DNA stuff, if you compared your human DNA to your mom's DNA, it would be a 50% match. Yes, the rest of it would be a 99.9% percent match, but the part that we actually care about would be 50%. This is what is actually happening here.</p>
</div>
