			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4450320">
									

<p>I like it! It's a pretty well written article in my opinion, but I would like to see the DNA copying aspect of the SCP explored a little more in depth. After all, being able to get someone's DNA from something as detaches as someone's memory of the person is a pretty big deal!</p>
<p>It's a nice twist, and I understand your inclination towards putting it at the very end of the article, but I think it would benefit more if it was expanded. If you still want to keep it as a twist, maybe put it as an update to a previous version of the (in universe) article? Like MaliceAforethought pointed out, that's not really how DNA works, but you can easily fix that by expanding onto the idea.</p>
<p>There's a lot of questions one could ask about this aspect of the SCP. What is the DNA being used for? Where is the SCP's &quot;actual&quot; DNA being stored, if it has any? Does the DNA of different kind of people have an effect on the growth of the SCP? Just to name a few.</p>
<p>Overall, great concept and a +1 from me!</p>

